  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A zener diode of power rating <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> is to be used as a voltage regulator. If the zener diode has a breakdown of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and it has to regulate voltage fluctuated between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></math> for safe operation should be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8433487d-7b09-455a-a663-d2fd4ae913eb-16de8932-8de0-400a-8197-5cbe63710257-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 138px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "20",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For diode <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>Now for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Voltage drop across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>iR</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#937;</mi></math></p>",
